From 4bf3c02a639e8e44d8598160c9f792a0727063f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 12:01:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06899/11362] [outer-loop] lf52: round 7 honest null, L7 mapped
 (fable-5)

claude-fable-5 round-7 session confirmed the game has win_levels=10
total (four levels remain beyond the banked frontier), then mapped L7's
west screen in detail: it is fully move-locked at level start (every
piece is a silent click), so the unlock chain must start on the unseen
east screen (a second peg + four more carriers, unexplored). Banked
the full west-screen carrier network (corridor entry/exit ferry,
bidirectional elevator line), the bottom-corridor socket layout
(sockets 5-9 contiguous, likely needing the two stacked red blocks as
stepping-stones), the grid<->frame coordinate mapping, and flagged
ACTION7's semantics as unresolved (not a simple undo).

Independently re-verified: replayed the 615-action L6 prefix from a
fresh env.reset() (level=6, state=GameState.NOT_FINISHED, matches
registry) and replayed the full 669-action session sequence to confirm
it does not cross into L7 either. No new level banked; frontier stays
at level 6. Budget was the binding constraint (615 of 690 actions
consumed by the prefix alone, leaving ~75 for exploration) -- next
attempt needs a larger budget or an L7-scoped keyhole reset.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
